Five pentagons through every edge: a vertex Moore ball
=====================================================

Scope and existing work
-----------------------

The fixed F012 Table 2 (physical page 18) claims n(4,5,5)=24 and exactly
one isomorphism class at that order. The already accepted positive witness
is UntilOrder250_115. Both the lower24 and uniqueness clause remain pending
in ledger40. The accepted quartic_girth_five component supplies the Moore
ball argument, but its complete enumeration is for lambda6/order20 only.
The matching_forest component supplies a general theorem for arbitrary
branch graph H; it is not restricted to its earlier bipartite application.
No source claim or new theorem is credited by this working note.

The three root patterns
-----------------------

Choose a vertex r in a quartic graph of girth five. Its Moore ball consists
of r, four neighbours u_i, and three leaves X_i adjacent to each u_i.
All seventeen vertices are distinct, and the root and its neighbours have
full degree. Additional edges of the induced ball therefore join leaves
of different branches. Between X_i and X_j these edges form a matching:
two neighbours in the same other branch give a quadrangle through its
parent. There are no additional restrictions at the level of matching
sizes; all graph girth restrictions must still be checked.

Every pentagon through edge r u_i consists of that edge, a leaf-parent
edge in branch i, one cross edge, one leaf-parent edge in another branch
and its edge to r. Thus the total number of cross edges incident with X_i
is exactly five. Write k_ij for each matching size. Each of four row sums
of this symmetric zero-diagonal matrix is five. Subtracting sums gives
k_01=k_23, k_02=k_13, k_03=k_12. For example twice(k_01-k_23) is the sum
of rows 0 and1 minus rows2 and3. Each size is between zero and three.

Put a=k_01, b=k_02 and c=k_03. Then a+b+c=5. Permuting the four branches
induces every permutation of the three opposite-edge pairs. Therefore
there are just three unordered triples: (0,2,3), (1,1,3), (1,2,2).
The twelve literal size vectors and their three S4 orbits are exhaustively
checked by the integer inventory. For each representative, apply the
acquired matching-forest theorem on H=K4 with four three-element sets.
The chosen forest gives respectively 54, 2187 and39366 matching assignments,
a total of41607, before testing girth. Every leaf permutation in the theorem
extends to an actual permutation of the Moore ball fixing its four parents
and root. Thus it preserves extendibility and all graph conditions.

The root enumeration must inspect all these literal assignments and reject
any triangle or quadrangle. A stored root may stand for another only after
a literal adjacency-preserving bijection respecting root/parent/leaf roles
is checked. A graph-isomorphism library may propose maps; no unchecked
canonical label is a certificate.

The exterior and the four relevant orders
----------------------------------------

The twelve leaves have36 slots beyond their parent edges. Ten cross edges
consume20 of them, leaving16 exterior incidences. If the exterior has t
vertices and e internal edges, then4t=16+2e, hence e=2t-8. In particular
n=17+t is at least21. To prove the source minimum and uniqueness it is
enough to complete the root at (t,e)=(4,0),(5,2),(6,4),(7,6).

The exterior is a finite simple graph H of girth at least five and maximum
degree at most four. There are at most binom(binom(7,2),6)=54264 labelled
six-edge graphs at the largest order. A complete exterior inventory can
therefore be obtained independently by enumerating every labelled edge
subset at each of the four orders and retaining its actual degree/girth
conditions. As for roots, any reduction to stored exterior representatives
must include a checked literal isomorphism. The inventory is not presumed
to contain only trees at t=7: pentagons and hexagons are possible and must
be retained.

Fix an actual root R and actual exterior H. An exterior vertex y with
H-degree h_y must receive precisely4-h_y neighbours among the twelve
leaves. It may meet each branch at most once, or a quadrangle would result.
Thus the remaining graph is specified by one subset B_y of those leaves
for every y. Each leaf must occur precisely its remaining degree, and
there are no unknown edges after all these subsets are assigned.

A complete constructor may choose these subsets in any fixed vertex order,
provided every subset of the required size with at most one leaf per branch
is visited. It may reject a negative leaf capacity, an impossible remaining
capacity sum, or an inserted edge whose endpoints already have a path of
length at most three. Each is a necessary condition on a subgraph of any
completion. At the end all degrees are four and girth is at least five.
For every edge, counting simple paths of length four between its endpoints
counts its pentagons exactly. Retain it if and only if every count is five.

Exact pentagon budgets
----------------------

Maintain for every present edge its exact number of pentagons in the
current partial graph. Initially this is counted by all simple paths of
length four between its endpoints. When a new edge uv is inserted, every
new pentagon contains uv, and removing uv gives a unique simple path of
length four from u to v in the previous graph. Enumerate those paths before
insertion. Their number is the count for uv; for each old edge add the
number of those paths containing it. This maintains exact counts by
induction. Reversing these recorded increments restores the previous graph
and every count exactly. Pentagons cannot disappear when more edges are
added. It is therefore necessary to reject any insertion giving a count
greater than five on any edge. The separate distance test rejects paths of
length at most three before insertion, preserving girth at least five.
Neither rejection excludes a subgraph of a required completion.

Exterior automorphisms
----------------------

For a fixed exterior H, enumerate every permutation of its at most seven
vertices and retain it precisely when all adjacency entries are preserved.
These are all of Aut(H), with no group recognition premise. Let B_y be the
leaf subset assigned to y, encoded by its twelve-bit mask. Order full
vectors (B_0,...,B_(t-1)) lexicographically. Every assignment has an orbit
minimum under these actual exterior automorphisms. An automorphism fixes
the old Moore ball and relabels the exterior, so it preserves every degree,
girth and pentagon requirement.

During the recursion compare the current masks with each permuted vector,
from coordinate zero upward. Stop that comparison at the first coordinate
where either mask is not assigned. Earlier equal coordinates remain equal
in any completion. If an assigned first difference is greater on the
current side, every completion of that partial assignment is greater than
its image and cannot be the orbit minimum. Rejecting it is safe. If it is
smaller, that comparison gives no rejection. In particular every prefix
of the global minimum survives, regardless of the chosen recursion order
(descending exterior degree, then label). At a full assignment the test is
exact lexicographic minimality, and therefore retains precisely one vector
per orbit. Later choices are otherwise exhaustive; no unproved symmetry
of leaf labels is used by this completion step.

Current computation boundary
----------------------------

The 41,607 root assignments are completely inspected; 15,270 have the
required girth and map literally to 348 retained roots. The exterior
inventories have respectively 1, 2, 6 and 12 classes, obtained from all
labelled edge subsets with checked maps. The cycle-budget implementation
has been compared with an independent five-vertex-cycle oracle on every
five-vertex graph and three budgets, including complete insertion and
rollback, and against the positive source graph.

The boundary target has not run. A successful complete call must cover
all 348 roots and all 21 exterior models and verify every returned graph
by literal adjacency maps. No failed or truncated call supplies exclusion
or uniqueness. Code normalization controls and a guided actual source
completion are being checked before allocating that bounded call.
